The '''''Marauder''''' was a modified [[Omicron-class attack shuttle|''Omicron''-class attack shuttle]] that served as the personal [[starship]] of [[Clone Force 99]], also known as the "Bad Batch." The craft was unique compared to other [[Grand Army of the Republic]] starships, so it was used for the Bad Batch's covert and undercover missions throughout the [[Clone Wars]]. Around [[18 BBY]], it was destroyed by [[CX-2]] on [[Pabu island|Pabu]].

==History==
{{Quote|Wrecker, easy with my ship.''"<br />"''Your ship?|Tech and Wrecker, while repairing the ''Marauder''|<ref name="Cornered" />}}
[[File:Marauder-RoR.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Marauder'' with wings opened in flight configuration.]]
The ''Marauder'' was utilized by [[Clone Force 99]] during the [[Clone Wars]]. After the execution of [[Order 66]] and the end of the war, the "Bad Batch" returned to the [[Cloning|clone]] [[Planet|homeworld]] [[Kamino]]. However, the group fled from the [[Galactic Empire]]'s new reign aboard the ''Marauder'', losing their companion [[Crosshair|CT-9904]] "Crosshair," who joined the Empire after having his [[behavioral modification biochip]]'s effects enhanced, and gaining one in [[Omega]], a young, enhanced clone who had previously spent her days as a medical assistant to the [[Kaminoan]] [[Nala Se]].<ref name="Aftermath" />

After traveling to [[Saleucami]] to meet with [[Cut Lawquane]], [[Tech]] and [[Echo]] decided to get the ship intentionally impounded by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] forces as part of their plan to help Cut and his family escape the [[planet]]. The ship would suffer damage in their escape,<ref name="Cut and Run" /> which caused them to drop out of [[hyperspace]] and make repairs on the [[Ordo Moon]]. As repairs were made on the exterior of the ship, [[Wrecker]] took the opportunity to work on the inside, fashioning the Bad Batch's newest companion, [[Omega]], a [[Omega's Room|room]] of her own by reconfiguring the ship's gunner's nest.<ref name="Replacements">{{TBB|Replacements}}</ref>

<div style="float:right">[[File:Marauder-Rampage.png|thumb|left|250px|The ''Marauder'' landing on Ord Mantell]]</div>
As the group worked on their next move, Echo informed them that he had overheard comm chatter placing the ship on the wanted list. They made for the [[moon]] [[Pantora]] to refuel, resupply, and scramble the ship's [[Magnetic signature|signature]], but the ship was recognized by the [[Sullustan]] [[Raspar Six]], who informed the [[bounty hunter]] [[Fennec Shand]] of their presence. After a chase, [[Hunter]] and Omega escaped the bounty hunter and the group quickly departed Pantora.<ref name="Cornered" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|I suggest we use our transport; not the most luxurious ride in the galaxy, but it doesn't scream 'Republic' like the rest of these.|Hunter in an unfinished version of "The Bad Batch"|<ref name="Story Reel">{{SW|url=video/the-bad-batch-star-wars-the-clone-wars-story-reel|text=Star Wars: The Clone Wars - Story Reel: The Bad Batch|nolive=1}}</ref>}}
[[File:HavocMarauder-StoryReels.png|thumb|left|200px|The ''Havoc Marauder'', with the pin-up of Padmé Amidala.]]
The ''Marauder'' first appeared in the unreleased, development version of the [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars: A Galaxy Divided|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'']] episode "[[The Bad Batch (episode)|The Bad Batch]]," and later appeared in the unfinished versions of subsequent episodes. The ship appeared again in the finished releases of the arc, streaming on [[Disney+]] starting [[February 21]], [[2020]].<ref name="BadBatch" />

In the unfinished version of "[[A Distant Echo]]," the vessel had nose art depicting [[Naboo]] [[senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]] in a provocative fashion with the subtitle "Good to be Bad."<ref name="Databank2018" /> However, in the finished version of the episode (and by extension, its other completed appearances), the nose art is no longer present.<ref name="ADistantEcho">In the [[Disney+]] release of "[[A Distant Echo]]," the nose art that was present in the development version of the episode is no longer visible.</ref>

The original entry for the ship in the official [[StarWars.com]] [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] that corresponded with the unfinished ''The Clone Wars'' episodes named the ship as ''Havoc Marauder''. This entry is no longer live.<ref name="Databank2018" /> However, with the release of ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'', the ship was renamed to simply the ''Marauder'' and all references to "Havoc" were removed from the Databank and all episode guides,<ref name="Databank2021" /> except the one for Clone Force 99.<ref name="Clone Force 99">{{Databank|clone-force-99-bad-batch|Clone Force 99 / The Bad Batch}}</ref> Despite this, the [[2022]] [[De Agostini]] booklet "[[Republic and Separatist Ships (2)|Ships of the Republic and Separatists (II)]]" referred to the ship as the ''Havoc Marauder''.<ref name="DeAgo SWE:RASS" /> According to [[Leland Chee]], the ''Marauder'' was renamed during the production of [[The Clone Wars: Season Seven|''The Clone Wars'': Season Seven]].<ref name="Tweet">{{Twitter|HolocronKeeper|status/1490850613596495878|[[Leland Chee]]|quote=I don't know the exact reasons for the change, but I do know we started internal messaging about the change prior to the release Clone Wars Season 7.|archivedate=20220221142845}}</ref> As of ''The Bad Batch''{{'s}} [[The Bad Batch Season 2|second season]] [[Spoils of War|premiere]], the name ''Marauder'' is used in dialogue, but the descriptive audio continues to refer to the ship by its original name.<ref name="Spoils of War">{{TBB|Spoils of War}}</ref> A ''[[Star Wars: Galaxy of Heroes]]'' kit reveal for the ''Marauder'' affirmed that it was renamed.<ref name="Kit Reveal">{{EA|url=games/starwars/galaxy-of-heroes/news/kit-reveal-marauder|text=Kit Reveal - Marauder}}</ref> Although in [[2022]], the ship had its original name intact in the ''[[Star Wars: Micro Galaxy Squadron]]'' toyline for Series 2.<ref name="Micro Galaxy">{{WebCite|url=https://www.rebelscale.com/star-wars-toys/micro-galaxy-squadron/series-2|text=Star Wars Micro Galaxy Squadron Series 2|archivedate=20241119114345}}</ref>

